# Chapter 08 independent cutover display review

Fixed source: 5c4ce6184f6d5fa817f472d202101aaf86af3195. Preparation f9b5a2f49f45dedf2b3345386c0eb51b3f0599e0 and its original manifest are retained unchanged. No tracked files were edited. This review does not implement or reauthorize editor operations described by the page.

Result: no additional blocking display/content finding in the tested scope. README bootstrap is not yet available and is not included as a pass.

The complete original Markdown and Doc were independently read for preparation. The final Doc equals that prepared source. Reversing only the four clarified heading literals reproduces every pre-move draft byte at 20caaf7. Their meanings and Kanji-only readings remain faithful to each original section; see preparation.md. All 11 original InlineCode strings match in order and bytes. The source retains 55 paragraphs, 10 Sections, 1,330 Ruby nodes and no table/list/link. This is a display review, not a fresh acceptance of the existing editor implementation or universal manuscript correctness.

Both generated HTML trees contain the same 11 files byte for byte; both Markdown trees contain the same 10 files. Every generated Markdown file equals the fixed commit. HTML receipts' source digests equal fixed Git inputs. Every declared artifact digest is verified. Source and artifact bytes/hashes are in input-hashes.json; browser tests serve independent scratch copies under two non-root paths.

Chromium, Firefox and WebKit each passed 375px and 1280px widths at both paths, with page JavaScript disabled: 12 cases, 120 semantic moves. Every case compares all 55 paragraph base strings, 11 headings, 11 code strings, the 1,330 visible Ruby nodes, no links/tables/lists, unique semantic IDs, real local stylesheet presence, zero page scripts, zero failed/nonlocal requests and no horizontal page overflow. Local HTML deliberately has semantic n- IDs only; old Markdown aliases are not required there.

The fixed public GitHub URL is https://github.com/neknaj/NEPL3/blob/5c4ce6184f6d5fa817f472d202101aaf86af3195/doc/spec/08-editor.md . The actual server rawLines equal fixed Git Markdown bytes. Its displayed all-notes text equals all 55 Doc paragraphs and 11 headings including every Ruby reading, and its 11 code strings are exact. The 21 empty alias paragraphs are explicitly counted separately. All 11 legacy aliases and 10 semantic anchors are unique and move to stable visible positions. The old pre-cutover server rawLines and actual 11 old permalink anchors were independently recovered at f9b5a2f and match the alias configuration.

All 11 automatic GitHub heading IDs are distinct from the 21 explicit names, with no repeated ID or name. In particular the snapshot/relations/lsp/trust clarifications produce distinct automatic heading IDs, while preserving old aliases. github-elements.json stores the actual DOM nodes; github-collisions.json stores the comparison.

Root separately reported a reload/layout race in its navigation precondition. The independent main run did not reproduce it. A dedicated additional probe reuses one loaded GitHub document, explicitly observes a stable offscreen target before navigation, then requires native fragment navigation to a stable visible target and a nonzero scroll displacement for every one of the 21 fragments. All passed. It records each precondition attempt and post-navigation observation. This does not treat root's earlier failed probe as a success or require ambient GitHub requests to reach network idle before a native fragment move.

Visual inspection: WebKit 375px body and all four clarified headings, Chromium 375px relations body were viewed directly. Their readings, wrapped code and base text are legible in these captures without overlap or clipping; relations' final okurigana wraps onto a second line and remains visible. A separate WebKit probe compares every base/reading pair and checks every nonblank article text node's rectangles against the 375px viewport. These pass. This is not a universal font, assistive-technology or user-comfort assessment. Exact browser versions/executable hashes and Python/Playwright versions are recorded in environment.json. The environment is the explicitly available project Playwright installation; it is not a claim that an unavailable in-app browser was used.

Pending: README verbatim restoration and offline 11-file bootstrap, final CI/integration, and any broader canonical migration acceptance remain separate. No budgets, source content, aliases or renderer were changed by this reviewer. PowerShell-generated raw logs retain their original encoding bytes. Copies used for serving and Python bytecode caches are excluded from the compact evidence manifest; their input identities are recorded separately.
